=head2 Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::Finding

Represents a piece of potentially sensitive content.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->name() >> / C<< $msg->name($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Resource name in format
projects/{project}/locations/{location}/findings/{finding} Populated only
when viewing persisted findings.

=item * C<< $msg->quote() >> / C<< $msg->quote($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The content that was found. Even if the content is not textual, it
may be converted to a textual representation here.
Provided if `include_quote` is true and the finding is
less than or equal to 4096 bytes long. If the finding exceeds 4096 bytes
in length, the quote may be omitted.

=item * C<< $msg->info_type() >> / C<< $msg->info_type($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Storage::InfoType>)

The type of content that might have been found.
Provided if `excluded_types` is false.

=item * C<< $msg->likelihood() >> / C<< $msg->likelihood($value) >>

Type: C<Enum> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Likelihood>)

Confidence of how likely it is that the `info_type` is correct.

=item * C<< $msg->location() >> / C<< $msg->location($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::Location>)

Where the content was found.

=item * C<< $msg->create_time() >> / C<< $msg->create_time($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Protobuf::Timestamp::Timestamp>)

Timestamp when finding was detected.

=item * C<< $msg->quote_info() >> / C<< $msg->quote_info($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::QuoteInfo>)

Contains data parsed from quotes. Only populated if include_quote was set
to true and a supported infoType was requested. Currently supported
infoTypes: DATE, DATE_OF_BIRTH and TIME.

=item * C<< $msg->resource_name() >> / C<< $msg->resource_name($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The job that stored the finding.

=item * C<< $msg->trigger_name() >> / C<< $msg->trigger_name($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Job trigger name, if applicable, for this finding.

=item * C<< $msg->labels() >> / C<< $msg->labels($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::Finding::LabelsEntry>)

The labels associated with this `Finding`.

Label keys must be between 1 and 63 characters long and must conform
to the following regular expression: `[a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?`.

Label values must be between 0 and 63 characters long and must conform
to the regular expression `([a-z]([-a-z0-9]*[a-z0-9])?)?`.

No more than 10 labels can be associated with a given finding.

Examples:

* `"environment" : "production"`
* `"pipeline" : "etl"`

=item * C<< $msg->job_create_time() >> / C<< $msg->job_create_time($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Protobuf::Timestamp::Timestamp>)

Time the job started that produced this finding.

=item * C<< $msg->job_name() >> / C<< $msg->job_name($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The job that stored the finding.

=item * C<< $msg->finding_id() >> / C<< $msg->finding_id($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The unique finding id.

=back

