=head2 Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::DateShiftConfig

Shifts dates by random number of days, with option to be consistent for the
same context. See
https://docs.cloud.google.com/sensitive-data-protection/docs/concepts-date-shifting
to learn more.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->upper_bound_days() >> / C<< $msg->upper_bound_days($value) >>

Type: C<Int32>

Required. Range of shift in days. Actual shift will be selected at random
within this range (inclusive ends). Negative means shift to earlier in
time. Must not be more than 365250 days (1000 years) each direction.

For example, 3 means shift date to at most 3 days into the future.

=item * C<< $msg->lower_bound_days() >> / C<< $msg->lower_bound_days($value) >>

Type: C<Int32>

Required. For example, -5 means shift date to at most 5 days back in the
past.

=item * C<< $msg->context() >> / C<< $msg->context($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Storage::FieldId>)

Points to the field that contains the context, for example, an entity id.
If set, must also set cryptoKey. If set, shift will be consistent for the
given context.

=item * C<< $msg->crypto_key() >> / C<< $msg->crypto_key($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::CryptoKey>)

Causes the shift to be computed based on this key and the context. This
results in the same shift for the same context and crypto_key. If
set, must also set context. Can only be applied to table items.

=back

=head2 Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::InfoTypeTransformations

A type of transformation that will scan unstructured text and
