=head2 Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::TransformationDescription

A flattened description of a `PrimitiveTransformation` or
`RecordSuppression`.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->type() >> / C<< $msg->type($value) >>

Type: C<Enum> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::TransformationType>)

The transformation type.

=item * C<< $msg->description() >> / C<< $msg->description($value) >>

Type: C<String>

A description of the transformation. This is empty for a
RECORD_SUPPRESSION, or is the output of calling toString() on the
`PrimitiveTransformation` protocol buffer message for any other type of
transformation.

=item * C<< $msg->condition() >> / C<< $msg->condition($value) >>

Type: C<String>

A human-readable string representation of the `RecordCondition`
corresponding to this transformation. Set if a `RecordCondition` was used
to determine whether or not to apply this transformation.

Examples:
    * (age_field > 85)
    * (age_field <= 18)
    * (zip_field exists)
    * (zip_field == 01234) && (city_field != "Springville")
    * (zip_field == 01234) && (age_field <= 18) && (city_field exists)

=item * C<< $msg->info_type() >> / C<< $msg->info_type($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Storage::InfoType>)

Set if the transformation was limited to a specific `InfoType`.

=back

=head2 Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::TransformationDetails

Details about a single transformation. This object contains a description of
the transformation, information about whether the transformation was
successfully applied, and the precise location where the transformation
occurred. These details are stored in a user-specified BigQuery table.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->resource_name() >> / C<< $msg->resource_name($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The name of the job that completed the transformation.

=item * C<< $msg->container_name() >> / C<< $msg->container_name($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The top level name of the container where the transformation is located
(this will be the source file name or table name).

=item * C<< $msg->transformation() >> / C<< $msg->transformation($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::TransformationDescription>)

Description of transformation. This would only contain more than one
element if there were multiple matching transformations and which one to
apply was ambiguous. Not set for states that contain no transformation,
currently only state that contains no transformation is
TransformationResultStateType.METADATA_UNRETRIEVABLE.

=item * C<< $msg->status_details() >> / C<< $msg->status_details($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::TransformationResultStatus>)

Status of the transformation, if transformation was not successful, this
will specify what caused it to fail, otherwise it will show that the
transformation was successful.

=item * C<< $msg->transformed_bytes() >> / C<< $msg->transformed_bytes($value) >>

Type: C<Int64>

The number of bytes that were transformed. If transformation was
unsuccessful or did not take place because there was no content to
transform, this will be zero.

=item * C<< $msg->transformation_location() >> / C<< $msg->transformation_location($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::TransformationLocation>)

The precise location of the transformed content in the original container.

=back

=head2 Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::TransformationLocation

Specifies the location of a transformation.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->finding_id() >> / C<< $msg->finding_id($value) >>

Type: C<String>

For infotype transformations, link to the corresponding findings ID so
that location information does not need to be duplicated. Each findings
ID correlates to an entry in the findings output table, this table only
gets created when users specify to save findings (add the save findings
action to the request).

=item * C<< $msg->record_transformation() >> / C<< $msg->record_transformation($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::RecordTransformation>)

For record transformations, provide a field and container information.

=item * C<< $msg->container_type() >> / C<< $msg->container_type($value) >>

Type: C<Enum> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::TransformationContainerType>)

Information about the functionality of the container where this finding
occurred, if available.

=back

=head2 Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::RecordTransformation

The field in a record to transform.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->field_id() >> / C<< $msg->field_id($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Storage::FieldId>)

For record transformations, provide a field.

=item * C<< $msg->container_timestamp() >> / C<< $msg->container_timestamp($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Protobuf::Timestamp::Timestamp>)

Findings container modification timestamp, if applicable.

=item * C<< $msg->container_version() >> / C<< $msg->container_version($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Container version, if available ("generation" for Cloud Storage).

=back

=head2 Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::TransformationResultStatus

The outcome of a transformation.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->result_status_type() >> / C<< $msg->result_status_type($value) >>

Type: C<Enum> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::TransformationResultStatusType>)

Transformation result status type, this will be either SUCCESS, or it will
be the reason for why the transformation was not completely successful.

=item * C<< $msg->details() >> / C<< $msg->details($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Rpc::Status::Status>)

Detailed error codes and messages

=back

=head2 Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::TransformationDetailsStorageConfig

Config for storing transformation details.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->table() >> / C<< $msg->table($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Storage::BigQueryTable>)

The BigQuery table in which to store the output. This may be an existing
table or in a new table in an existing dataset.
If table_id is not set a new one will be generated for you with the
following format:
dlp_googleapis_transformation_details_yyyy_mm_dd_[dlp_job_id]. Pacific
time zone will be used for generating the date details.

=back

=head2 Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::Schedule

Schedule for inspect job triggers.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->recurrence_period_duration() >> / C<< $msg->recurrence_period_duration($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Protobuf::Duration::Duration>)

With this option a job is started on a regular periodic basis. For
example: every day (86400 seconds).

A scheduled start time will be skipped if the previous
execution has not ended when its scheduled time occurs.

This value must be set to a time duration greater than or equal
to 1 day and can be no longer than 60 days.

=back

=head2 Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::Manual

Job trigger option for hybrid jobs. Jobs must be manually created
and finished.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head2 Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::InspectTemplate

The inspectTemplate contains a configuration (set of types of sensitive data
to be detected) to be used anywhere you otherwise would normally specify
InspectConfig. See
https://docs.cloud.google.com/sensitive-data-protection/docs/concepts-templates
to learn more.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->name() >> / C<< $msg->name($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Output only. The template name.

The template will have one of the following formats:
`projects/PROJECT_ID/inspectTemplates/TEMPLATE_ID` OR
`organizations/ORGANIZATION_ID/inspectTemplates/TEMPLATE_ID`;

=item * C<< $msg->display_name() >> / C<< $msg->display_name($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Display name (max 256 chars).

=item * C<< $msg->description() >> / C<< $msg->description($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Short description (max 256 chars).

=item * C<< $msg->create_time() >> / C<< $msg->create_time($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Protobuf::Timestamp::Timestamp>)

Output only. The creation timestamp of an inspectTemplate.

=item * C<< $msg->update_time() >> / C<< $msg->update_time($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Protobuf::Timestamp::Timestamp>)

Output only. The last update timestamp of an inspectTemplate.

=item * C<< $msg->inspect_config() >> / C<< $msg->inspect_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::InspectConfig>)

The core content of the template. Configuration of the scanning process.

=item * C<< $msg->allow_limited_availability_info_types() >> / C<< $msg->allow_limited_availability_info_types($value) >>

Type: C<Bool>

Optional. Enables the use of [limited-availability built-in
infoTypes](https://docs.cloud.google.com/sensitive-data-protection/docs/infotypes-reference#limited-availability-infotypes)
in inspect_config. These infoTypes are supported only in specific regions
and can cause scanning errors if used elsewhere.

=back

