=head2 Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::DiscoveryConfig

Configuration for discovery to scan resources for profile generation.
Only one discovery configuration may exist per organization, folder,
or project.

The generated data profiles are retained according to the
[data retention policy]
(https://docs.cloud.google.com/sensitive-data-protection/docs/data-profiles#retention).

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->name() >> / C<< $msg->name($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Output only. Unique resource name for the DiscoveryConfig, assigned by the
service when the DiscoveryConfig is created, for example
`projects/dlp-test-project/locations/global/discoveryConfigs/53234423`.

=item * C<< $msg->display_name() >> / C<< $msg->display_name($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Display name (max 100 chars)

=item * C<< $msg->org_config() >> / C<< $msg->org_config($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::DiscoveryConfig::OrgConfig>)

Only set when the parent is an org.

=item * C<< $msg->other_cloud_starting_location() >> / C<< $msg->other_cloud_starting_location($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::OtherCloudDiscoveryStartingLocation>)

Must be set only when scanning other clouds.

=item * C<< $msg->inspect_templates() >> / C<< $msg->inspect_templates($value) >>

Type: C<String>

Detection logic for profile generation.

Not all template features are used by Discovery. FindingLimits,
include_quote and exclude_info_types have no impact on
Discovery.

Multiple templates may be provided if there is data in multiple regions.
At most one template must be specified per-region (including "global").
Each region is scanned using the applicable template. If no region-specific
template is specified, but a "global" template is specified, it will be
copied to that region and used instead. If no global or region-specific
template is provided for a region with data, that region's data will not be
scanned.

For more information, see
https://docs.cloud.google.com/sensitive-data-protection/docs/data-profiles#data-residency.

=item * C<< $msg->actions() >> / C<< $msg->actions($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::DataProfileAction>)

Actions to execute at the completion of scanning.

=item * C<< $msg->targets() >> / C<< $msg->targets($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::DiscoveryTarget>)

Target to match against for determining what to scan and how frequently.

=item * C<< $msg->errors() >> / C<< $msg->errors($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::Error>)

Output only. A stream of errors encountered when the config was activated.
Repeated errors may result in the config automatically being paused. Output
only field. Will return the last 100 errors. Whenever the config is
modified this list will be cleared.

=item * C<< $msg->create_time() >> / C<< $msg->create_time($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Protobuf::Timestamp::Timestamp>)

Output only. The creation timestamp of a DiscoveryConfig.

=item * C<< $msg->update_time() >> / C<< $msg->update_time($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Protobuf::Timestamp::Timestamp>)

Output only. The last update timestamp of a DiscoveryConfig.

=item * C<< $msg->last_run_time() >> / C<< $msg->last_run_time($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Protobuf::Timestamp::Timestamp>)

Output only. The timestamp of the last time this config was executed.

=item * C<< $msg->status() >> / C<< $msg->status($value) >>

Type: C<Enum> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::DiscoveryConfig::Status>)

Required. A status for this configuration.

=item * C<< $msg->processing_location() >> / C<< $msg->processing_location($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::ProcessingLocation>)

Optional. Processing location configuration. Vertex AI dataset scanning
will set processing_location.image_fallback_type to MultiRegionProcessing
by default.

=back

=head3 Enum: DiscoveryConfig::Status

=over 4

=item * C<STATUS_UNSPECIFIED> => C<0>

=item * C<RUNNING> => C<1>

=item * C<PAUSED> => C<2>

=back

=head2 Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::DiscoveryTarget

Target used to match against for Discovery.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->big_query_target() >> / C<< $msg->big_query_target($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::BigQueryDiscoveryTarget>)

BigQuery target for Discovery. The first target to match a table will be
the one applied.

=item * C<< $msg->cloud_sql_target() >> / C<< $msg->cloud_sql_target($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::CloudSqlDiscoveryTarget>)

Cloud SQL target for Discovery. The first target to match a table will be
the one applied.

=item * C<< $msg->secrets_target() >> / C<< $msg->secrets_target($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::SecretsDiscoveryTarget>)

Discovery target that looks for credentials and secrets stored in cloud
resource metadata and reports them as vulnerabilities to Security Command
Center. Only one target of this type is allowed.

=item * C<< $msg->cloud_storage_target() >> / C<< $msg->cloud_storage_target($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::CloudStorageDiscoveryTarget>)

Cloud Storage target for Discovery. The first target to match a table
will be the one applied.

=item * C<< $msg->other_cloud_target() >> / C<< $msg->other_cloud_target($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::OtherCloudDiscoveryTarget>)

Other clouds target for discovery. The first target to match a resource
will be the one applied.

=item * C<< $msg->vertex_dataset_target() >> / C<< $msg->vertex_dataset_target($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::VertexDatasetDiscoveryTarget>)

Vertex AI dataset target for Discovery. The first target to match a
dataset will be the one applied. Note that discovery for Vertex AI can
incur Cloud Storage Class B operation charges for storage.objects.get
operations and retrieval fees. For more information, see [Cloud Storage
pricing](https://cloud.google.com/storage/pricing#price-tables).
Note that discovery for Vertex AI dataset will not be able to scan images
unless DiscoveryConfig.processing_location.image_fallback_location has
multi_region_processing or global_processing configured.

=back

=head2 Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::BigQueryDiscoveryTarget

Target used to match against for discovery with BigQuery tables

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->filter() >> / C<< $msg->filter($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::DiscoveryBigQueryFilter>)

Required. The tables the discovery cadence applies to. The first target
with a matching filter will be the one to apply to a table.

=item * C<< $msg->conditions() >> / C<< $msg->conditions($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::DiscoveryBigQueryConditions>)

In addition to matching the filter, these conditions must be true
before a profile is generated.

=item * C<< $msg->cadence() >> / C<< $msg->cadence($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::DiscoveryGenerationCadence>)

How often and when to update profiles. New tables that match both the
filter and conditions are scanned as quickly as possible depending on
system capacity.

=item * C<< $msg->disabled() >> / C<< $msg->disabled($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::Disabled>)

Tables that match this filter will not have profiles created.

=back

=head2 Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::DiscoveryBigQueryFilter

Determines what tables will have profiles generated within an organization
or project. Includes the ability to filter by regular expression patterns
on project ID, dataset ID, and table ID.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->tables() >> / C<< $msg->tables($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::BigQueryTableCollection>)

A specific set of tables for this filter to apply to. A table collection
must be specified in only one filter per config.
If a table id or dataset is empty, Cloud DLP assumes all tables in that
collection must be profiled. Must specify a project ID.

=item * C<< $msg->other_tables() >> / C<< $msg->other_tables($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::DiscoveryBigQueryFilter::AllOtherBigQueryTables>)

Catch-all. This should always be the last filter in the list because
anything above it will apply first. Should only appear once in a
configuration. If none is specified, a default one will be added
automatically.

=item * C<< $msg->table_reference() >> / C<< $msg->table_reference($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Storage::TableReference>)

The table to scan. Discovery configurations including this can only
include one DiscoveryTarget (the DiscoveryTarget with this
TableReference).

=back

