=back

=head2 Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::DiscoveryBigQueryConditions

Requirements that must be true before a table is scanned in discovery for the
first time. There is an AND relationship between the top-level attributes.
Additionally, minimum conditions with an OR relationship that must be met
before Cloud DLP scans a table can be set (like a minimum row count or a
minimum table age).

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->created_after() >> / C<< $msg->created_after($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Protobuf::Timestamp::Timestamp>)

BigQuery table must have been created after this date. Used to avoid
backfilling.

=item * C<< $msg->types() >> / C<< $msg->types($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::BigQueryTableTypes>)

Restrict discovery to specific table types.

=item * C<< $msg->type_collection() >> / C<< $msg->type_collection($value) >>

Type: C<Enum> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::BigQueryTableTypeCollection>)

Restrict discovery to categories of table types.

=item * C<< $msg->or_conditions() >> / C<< $msg->or_conditions($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::DiscoveryBigQueryConditions::OrConditions>)

At least one of the conditions must be true for a table to be scanned.

=back

