=head2 Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::DiscoveryCloudSqlGenerationCadence

How often existing tables should have their profiles refreshed.
New tables are scanned as quickly as possible depending on system
capacity.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->schema_modified_cadence() >> / C<< $msg->schema_modified_cadence($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::DiscoveryCloudSqlGenerationCadence::SchemaModifiedCadence>)

When to reprofile if the schema has changed.

=item * C<< $msg->refresh_frequency() >> / C<< $msg->refresh_frequency($value) >>

Type: C<Enum> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::DataProfileUpdateFrequency>)

Data changes (non-schema changes) in Cloud SQL tables can't trigger
reprofiling. If you set this field, profiles are refreshed at this
