=head2 Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::FileStoreDataProfile

The profile for a file store.

* Cloud Storage: maps 1:1 with a bucket.
* Amazon S3: maps 1:1 with a bucket.

Inherits from L<Protobuf::Message>.

=head3 Accessors

=over 4

=item * C<< $msg->name() >> / C<< $msg->name($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The name of the profile.

=item * C<< $msg->data_source_type() >> / C<< $msg->data_source_type($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::DataSourceType>)

The resource type that was profiled.

=item * C<< $msg->project_data_profile() >> / C<< $msg->project_data_profile($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The resource name of the project data profile for this file store.

=item * C<< $msg->project_id() >> / C<< $msg->project_id($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The Google Cloud project ID that owns the resource.
For Amazon S3 buckets, this is the AWS Account Id.

=item * C<< $msg->file_store_location() >> / C<< $msg->file_store_location($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The location of the file store.

* Cloud Storage:
https://docs.cloud.google.com/storage/docs/locations#available-locations
* Amazon S3:
https://docs.aws.amazon.com/general/latest/gr/rande.html#regional-endpoints

=item * C<< $msg->data_storage_locations() >> / C<< $msg->data_storage_locations($value) >>

Type: C<String>

For resources that have multiple storage locations, these are those
regions. For Cloud Storage this is the list of regions chosen for
dual-region storage. `file_store_location` will normally be the
corresponding multi-region for the list of individual locations. The first
region is always picked as the processing and storage location for the data
profile.

=item * C<< $msg->location_type() >> / C<< $msg->location_type($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The location type of the file store (region, dual-region, multi-region,
etc). If dual-region, expect data_storage_locations to be populated.

=item * C<< $msg->file_store_path() >> / C<< $msg->file_store_path($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The file store path.

* Cloud Storage: `gs://{bucket}`
* Amazon S3: `s3://{bucket}`
* Vertex AI dataset:
`projects/{project_number}/locations/{location}/datasets/{dataset_id}`

=item * C<< $msg->full_resource() >> / C<< $msg->full_resource($value) >>

Type: C<String>

The resource name of the resource profiled.
https://cloud.google.com/apis/design/resource_names#full_resource_name

Example format of an S3 bucket full resource name:
`//cloudasset.googleapis.com/organizations/{org_id}/otherCloudConnections/aws/arn:aws:s3:::{bucket_name}`

=item * C<< $msg->config_snapshot() >> / C<< $msg->config_snapshot($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::DataProfileConfigSnapshot>)

The snapshot of the configurations used to generate the profile.

=item * C<< $msg->profile_status() >> / C<< $msg->profile_status($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::ProfileStatus>)

Success or error status from the most recent profile generation attempt.
May be empty if the profile is still being generated.

=item * C<< $msg->state() >> / C<< $msg->state($value) >>

Type: C<Enum> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::FileStoreDataProfile::State>)

State of a profile.

=item * C<< $msg->profile_last_generated() >> / C<< $msg->profile_last_generated($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Protobuf::Timestamp::Timestamp>)

The last time the profile was generated.

=item * C<< $msg->resource_visibility() >> / C<< $msg->resource_visibility($value) >>

Type: C<Enum> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::ResourceVisibility>)

How broadly a resource has been shared.

=item * C<< $msg->sensitivity_score() >> / C<< $msg->sensitivity_score($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Storage::SensitivityScore>)

The sensitivity score of this resource.

=item * C<< $msg->data_risk_level() >> / C<< $msg->data_risk_level($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::DataRiskLevel>)

The data risk level of this resource.

=item * C<< $msg->create_time() >> / C<< $msg->create_time($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Protobuf::Timestamp::Timestamp>)

The time the file store was first created.

=item * C<< $msg->last_modified_time() >> / C<< $msg->last_modified_time($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Protobuf::Timestamp::Timestamp>)

The time the file store was last modified.

=item * C<< $msg->file_cluster_summaries() >> / C<< $msg->file_cluster_summaries($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::FileClusterSummary>)

FileClusterSummary per each cluster.

=item * C<< $msg->resource_attributes() >> / C<< $msg->resource_attributes($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::FileStoreDataProfile::ResourceAttributesEntry>)

Attributes of the resource being profiled.
Currently used attributes:

* customer_managed_encryption: boolean
    - true: the resource is encrypted with a customer-managed key.
    - false: the resource is encrypted with a provider-managed key.

=item * C<< $msg->resource_labels() >> / C<< $msg->resource_labels($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::FileStoreDataProfile::ResourceLabelsEntry>)

The labels applied to the resource at the time the profile was generated.

=item * C<< $msg->file_store_info_type_summaries() >> / C<< $msg->file_store_info_type_summaries($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Dlp::FileStoreInfoTypeSummary>)

InfoTypes detected in this file store.

=item * C<< $msg->sample_findings_table() >> / C<< $msg->sample_findings_table($value) >>

Type: C<Message> (L<Google::Privacy::Dlp::V2::Storage::BigQueryTable>)

The BigQuery table to which the sample findings are written.

=item * C<< $msg->file_store_is_empty() >> / C<< $msg->file_store_is_empty($value) >>

Type: C<Bool>

The file store does not have any files. If the profiling operation failed,
